TASK: Restyle the UI component library in `../components/ui` (and every consumer that hard-codes styling) into a new visual language. Change appearance only. Do NOT change component names, props, behavior, exports, or file structure. Everything in the import list must keep working: AngleDial, Avatar, Badge, Banner, BarChart, BrandWordmark, Button, ButtonGroup, CapacityBadge, Checkbox, ColorField, ContextMenu, CurveRamp, DataGrid, Dialog, GaugeBar, Grid, Heatmap, Histogram, Icon, Inline, JobQueue, Kbd, Knob, LineChart, LogConsole, MenuBar, NodeGraph, NumberField, Panel, PasswordField, Popover, ProgressBar, PropertyEditor, RadioGroup, RadioItem, RangeSlider, ScatterPlot, ScrollArea, SearchField, SegmentedControl, Select, Separator, Slider, Sparkline, Spinner, Stack, StatusBar, StatusBarSegment, StatusDot, Stepper, Switch, Table, Tabs, Tag, Text, TextArea, TextField, Timebar, TokenTile, ToolStrip, Toolbar, ToolbarGroup, Tooltip, Topbar, TransportControls, UserPicker, VectorField, useToast.

CONTEXT: This is the UI kit of a VFX/animation production-tracking tool. The functional reference is the density and seriousness of Houdini and Nuke. The visual reference is the attached concept images: soft neumorphic "foundations" sheet, minimal tactile controls, and the audio-editor mockup with detailed knobs and tick rulers.

STYLE IN ONE SENTENCE: Matte paper-like surfaces that feel physically pressed in or popped out of the screen with very soft light/shadow, almost no corner rounding, and finely detailed controls (ticks, grooves, knurled knobs, LED dots) set in generous empty space. It should feel like a 2002 pro-software control panel, refined with modern restraint.

1. DESIGN TOKENS (do this first)
Centralize everything in one token file (CSS variables, or the existing theme system if there is one). Remove hard-coded colors from components afterwards.

Base neutrals:
  --bg-canvas: #1a1a1a   (viewers, timeline/calendar grid, deepest wells)
  --bg-app: #232323      (main window, center area)
  --bg-panel: #2b2b2b    (side panels, topbar)
  --bg-raised: #333333   (cards, table headers, toolbars)
  --bg-input: #1f1f1f    (fields, dropdowns, wells)
  --border: #3f3f3f
  --hover: #3a3a3a
  --selected: #3d4a5c
Text: --text #d4d4d4 (never pure white), --text-dim #9a9a9a, --text-off #5e5e5e.
Zone accents (muted, used only as signal): management #d98a4e (hover #e39c66, tint #3a2e25); production #5b93c7 (hover #74a6d4, tint #24303c); settings #8a8f96 (tint #2e3033). Focus/active: #e8a33d.
Status: WIP #e0b341, pending review #4fa3d9, approved #5fb36b, rejected #d95b5b, idle #6b7280. Show status as small chips, dots, or a 3px left bar with ~15% tinted background, never big solid fills.
Department colors (calendar/charts, desaturated, similar luminance): modeling #7a9cc6, rigging #9b86c4, animation #6fb3a0, lookdev #c79b6a, lighting #c4c06a, FX #c77a7a, comp #8fb86a.

Also create tokens for:
  - Radius: --r-0: 0, --r-1: 1px, --r-2: 2px. Max is 3px, used only on popovers/dialogs. Default is 0-2px. No pills, no circles except knobs, radios, avatars, and status dots.
  - Border widths: 1px thin (default), 2px regular (focus/active), 4px thick (rare emphasis).
  - Spacing scale on a 4px grid (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32). Control height 26-28px, compact rows 24px.
  - Elevation shadow recipes (below).
  - Motion: 120ms ease-out for press/hover, 180ms for popovers; no bounces.

2. SURFACE SYSTEM (the core idea, from the "Foundations" sheet)
Four physical layers. Light comes from the top-left. On dark, "light" means a faint 1px highlight on top/left edges and "shadow" means a soft darker falloff to bottom/right. Keep all shadows very soft, low opacity, and tight; nothing should look glossy or heavy.

  BASE (flat): background only, 1px --border, no shadow.
  RAISED (buttons, cards, toolbars, switch knobs, slider thumbs):
    box-shadow: inset 1px 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.05), inset -1px -1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.25), 1px 2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.35), -1px -1px 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.025);
  INSET (fields, wells, slider tracks, progress/gauge troughs, table body, log console):
    box-shadow: inset 1px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.55), inset -1px -1px 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
    background: --bg-input
  PRESSED (active button, toggled segment, selected tab):
    same as inset but a little lighter, and translateY(1px) with no outer shadow, so the element visibly sinks.
  POPOVER/MODAL: raised plus a larger, soft, very low-opacity drop (0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)), 1px border, radius up to 3px.

Elevation levels: L1 flat, L2 hover (shadow slightly stronger), L3 raised, L4 modal, L5 popover. Hover should only deepen the shadow by a hair and lighten the background to --hover. No color jumps.

Paper feel: add an extremely subtle noise/grain overlay (SVG feTurbulence or a tiny tiled PNG data-URI, opacity 2-4%) on --bg-app and --bg-panel so surfaces read as matte paper, not flat digital fills. No gradients except a barely visible vertical gradient (max 3% lightness difference) on raised controls to suggest a physical top face.

3. SHAPE AND BORDER RULES
  - Corners nearly square: 0-2px. Softness comes from shadows and tone, not from rounded corners.
  - 1px hairline borders in --border, always combined with the inner highlight, so edges look bevelled rather than outlined.
  - Replace thick outlines and heavy dividers with Separator as a 1px groove: a dark line (#1a1a1a) with a 1px light line (rgba(255,255,255,0.04)) directly beneath it.
  - Focus ring: 2px --focus outline with 1px offset plus a faint glow (0 0 0 3px rgba(232,163,61,0.18)).

4. TYPOGRAPHY
  UI font: Inter (fallback Segoe UI, system-ui), 11-12px base, weights 400/500/600 only. Labels in small caps or uppercase with 0.06em tracking for section titles, etched and subtle (--text-dim).
  Mono font: JetBrains Mono (fallback Roboto Mono) for versions, frame numbers, timecodes, paths, Kbd, NumberField, LogConsole, DataGrid numeric columns. Use tabular numerals everywhere numbers align.
  Text hierarchy through tone (--text / --text-dim / --text-off), not through size jumps.

5. DENSITY AND WHITESPACE (the 2002-meets-modern balance)
Controls are detailed but never crowded. Give every control generous clear space around it (min 8px gap between adjacent controls, 12-16px between groups, 24px between sections). Panels use real padding (12-16px). A screen should feel calm and sparse, with intricate controls sitting in open space like instruments on a panel. Group related controls into recessed or raised "plates" (Panel, ToolbarGroup) instead of lining everything with borders.

6. COMPONENT-LEVEL DIRECTION
Buttons and button-like (Button, ButtonGroup, SegmentedControl, ToolStrip, Toolbar, ToolbarGroup, TransportControls, Stepper):
  - Raised physical keys, 0-2px radius, subtle top highlight, soft bottom shadow. Pressed state sinks (inset + 1px down). Disabled: flat, no shadow, --text-off.
  - Primary variant uses the zone accent as a muted face tint or a small LED/underline, never a loud solid block. Destructive uses #d95b5b the same way.
  - ButtonGroup/SegmentedControl: one shared plate with hairline grooves between keys; the active segment is pressed in with a tiny accent indicator.
  - TransportControls: square keycap buttons like a tape deck/audio editor (see reference); record key has a small red dot (#d95b5b).
  - Add a micro-detail: a barely visible inner 1px border (rgba(255,255,255,0.03)) one pixel inside the edge for a machined look.

Switch, Checkbox, RadioGroup/RadioItem:
  - Switch: inset track (groove) with a raised rectangular or very softly rounded knob that slides; ON shows a small accent LED line or tinted track; OFF is neutral. Add tiny etched "I / O" or ON/OFF ticks if space allows.
  - Checkbox: small inset square well; checked shows a crisp thin check in the accent plus a faint inner glow. Radio: inset circular well with a raised/glowing dot when selected.

Sliders, Knobs, Dials (Slider, RangeSlider, Knob, AngleDial, CurveRamp, VectorField):
  - Slider track: deep inset groove with fine tick marks and numeric labels below (0/25/50/75/100 style, mono, --text-dim). Filled portion is a muted accent. Thumb is a raised key with a center grip line.
  - Knob/AngleDial: round raised dial with a knurled/ribbed edge (repeating-conic-gradient or SVG ticks), a soft cast shadow, a thin accent indicator line, and a tick ring around it with min/max labels, like the audio-editor reference. Pressed/dragging state darkens slightly.
  - RangeSlider uses two thumbs on the same groove with the active range tinted.

Fields (TextField, NumberField, PasswordField, SearchField, TextArea, Select, ColorField, UserPicker):
  - Inset wells on --bg-input, 1px border, placeholder in --text-off, value in --text. NumberField shows a small stepper pair and a draggable scrub area, with mono digits. Focus uses the focus ring above. Error state: 1px #d95b5b border with a faint red inner glow and helper text beneath. Select has a thin chevron glyph and a raised popover list.

Bars and meters (ProgressBar, GaugeBar, CapacityBadge, Sparkline, StatusBar, StatusBarSegment):
  - Recessed trough with a slightly raised fill, subtle segment ticks (like a hardware level meter). Fill colors follow status tokens. StatusBar is a thin docked strip with etched dividers and mono text. StatusDot is a tiny LED: solid color, 1px darker rim, soft glow (0 0 4px of its own color at 40%).

Navigation and structure (Topbar, MenuBar, Tabs, Panel, Separator, ScrollArea, ContextMenu, Popover, Tooltip, Dialog, Banner, useToast):
  - Topbar/MenuBar on --bg-panel with a 1px groove underline in the active zone's accent. Tabs: inactive tabs are flat, the active tab is pressed or raised into the panel with a thin accent line; no pill shapes.
  - Panel: raised plate with an etched small-caps header strip; optional collapsible state with a tiny chevron.
  - ContextMenu/Popover/Dialog: raised popover surface, small radius (max 3px), soft large shadow, hairline border; menu items are 24px with hover tint and mono Kbd hints right-aligned.
  - Tooltip: dark plate with tiny arrow, 11px text, short delay.
  - Banner: flat tinted strip with a 3px left status bar. Toasts: small raised cards stacked bottom-right with a left status bar.
  - ScrollArea: thin inset scrollbars with a raised square thumb, no rounded pills.

Data display (Table, DataGrid, PropertyEditor, JobQueue, LogConsole, Tag, Badge, Kbd, TokenTile, Avatar, Text, Grid, Stack, Inline):
  - Table/DataGrid: inset body on --bg-input or --bg-app, header as a raised strip with etched small-caps labels and sort glyphs, 24px rows, subtle zebra (1-2% lightness), selected row --selected, hover --hover, a 3px status bar at the row's left edge when a status applies. Column separators are groove lines.
  - PropertyEditor: label column (--text-dim) and value column with inset fields; group headers are collapsible etched strips.
  - Tag/Badge: tiny square-ish chips (0-2px radius), tinted background at ~15% with 1px matching border; CapacityBadge in mono.
  - Kbd: small raised keycap with 1px bottom shadow, mono text.
  - Avatar: square or very slightly rounded (2px) with a 1px bevel ring; no large circles.
  - JobQueue and LogConsole: console-like inset wells, mono text, status dots, colored log levels from the status tokens.

Charts and visualizations (BarChart, LineChart, Histogram, ScatterPlot, Heatmap, Sparkline, Timebar, NodeGraph, Gauge-style visuals):
  - Chart canvas uses --bg-canvas as an inset well with fine 1px grid lines (rgba(255,255,255,0.05)) and ruler-style tick labels in mono --text-dim. Series use the department/status palette, desaturated, thin 1.5px strokes, no gradients or glows (a faint 10-15% fill under lines at most). Timebar is a ruler with major/minor ticks like the reference. NodeGraph: rectangular nodes as raised plates with small port pills, thin #6b7280 connector lines, selected node gets the focus color outline; connectors can have tiny rounded elbows only.

Brand and icons (BrandWordmark, Icon, Spinner):
  - Icons: 1.5px stroke line icons, 16/20/24px grid, --text-dim by default, accent only when active; keep optical sizes consistent across the kit. Spinner is a thin segmented ring or tick-dial, not a thick circular arc.
  - BrandWordmark: keep the mark, restyle with the new text color and an etched/embossed treatment (1px dark shadow below, 1px light above).

7. INTERACTION AND MOTION
  Hover: background to --hover, shadow +1 level. Press: sink 1px, switch to inset recipe, 80-120ms. Selected/active: pressed look plus accent indicator. Disabled: flat, desaturated, no pointer. No springy animations; a physical, mechanical feel (quick ease-out, tiny travel). Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

8. ACCESSIBILITY
  Maintain WCAG AA contrast for text (--text on any surface, --text-dim only for secondary labels at 11px+ weight 500). Never rely on color alone for status: pair color with an icon, shape, or label. Keep visible focus states on every interactive component and keyboard operability unchanged.

9. HOW TO WORK
  a) Audit ../components/ui and list every hard-coded color, radius, shadow, and font; report before editing.
  b) Create/replace the token layer, then build the shared surface mixins/utilities (raised, inset, pressed, groove, grain, focus-ring) so components don't duplicate shadow strings.
  c) Restyle in this order: Button family -> fields -> switches/checkboxes/radios -> sliders/knobs -> bars/meters -> navigation/panels/overlays -> tables/data -> charts/graphs -> icons/wordmark.
  d) Keep a light "paper" theme as an optional second token set with the same structure (cream-gray paper base ~#ece8e1 / #e6e2da, ink text #2b2f33, deep teal/ink accent, same shadow logic with white highlights top-left and soft warm-gray shadows bottom-right) so the system can switch themes by swapping tokens only. The dark theme above is the default.
  e) If there is a storybook, demo, or gallery page, update it so every component and state (default, hover, pressed, focus, disabled, error, selected) is visible in one "Foundations/Controls/Navigation/Data/Feedback" layout like the first reference image.
  f) Run typecheck, lint, and the existing tests; fix regressions. Do not change public APIs.

10. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
  - At first glance the UI reads as a calm, matte, dark paper-like control panel with tactile controls that look pressed in or popped out by very soft shadows.
  - Corners are essentially square; no rounded "SaaS card" look.
  - Buttons, switches, sliders, knobs, and bars are visibly detailed (ticks, grooves, knurling, LED dots) yet surrounded by ample empty space.
  - All colors come from tokens; swapping to the light paper token set restyles the whole kit with no component edits.
  - No functional or API changes; build, types, and tests pass.